# Never in a build context.
#
# uploads/ was the one that mattered: 2.9 MB of real photos and stickers, and it
# was not ignored, so every file anybody uploaded changed the checksum of
# `COPY . .` and threw away the Go build cache. A single photo upload could cost
# a full dependency rebuild. It is a bind mount at runtime - the image does not
# need it - and no user data has any business in a build context.
uploads/
backups/

data/
bin/
*.db
*.db-wal
*.db-shm

# Local editor and VCS noise.
.git/
.idea/
.DS_Store

# Docs are not compiled. *.md also covers them, kept explicit because the rule
# above is about directories and this one is the habit worth naming.
*.md